<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#guerrilla-warfare">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guerrilla warfare</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as guerrilla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guerrilla warfare is a form of irregular warfare in which small, mobile forces use raids, ambushes and knowledge of terrain against larger conventional armies. It appears in the histories of many empires. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> was founded largely through such tactics, the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> movement used them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas Mountains</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> faced them in colonial conflicts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare.jpg" alt="Guerrilla warfare" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roque Gameiro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:As_Guerrilhas_na_Guerra_Peninsular_(Roque_Gameiro,_Quadros_da_Hist%C3%B3ria_de_Portugal,_1917).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
